Here's how to get the top 3 gaming genres from your customers collection:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;

public class GameGenreAggregator
{
    public static void GetTopGenres()
    {
        var customerCollection = new List<Customer>(); // Replace with actual data source

        var genrePurchases = customerCollection
            .SelectMany(c => c.Purchases)
            .GroupBy(p => p.Game.Genre)
            .OrderByDescending(g => g.Count())
            .Take(3);

        foreach (var genre in genrePurchases)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"Top Genre: {genre.Key}");

            // Get the first game of this genre
            var representativeGame = genre.First().Game;

            // Display wiki link for the genre
            Console.WriteLine($"Wiki Link: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/{representativeGame.Genre.ToLower()}");
        }
    }
}
```

This code will:
1. Group all purchases by their game's genre
2. Sort them by purchase count in descending order
3. Take the top 3 genres
4. Display each genre and its corresponding Wikipedia link

Note: You'll need to replace `new List<Customer>()` with your actual customer collection data source.

